355
00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:35.680
I was like, if there was a camera on me, I'd be like, oh, he's not acting.
我当时心想，如果当时有摄像机对着我，我会觉得，噢，他不是在演戏。

356
00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:37.280
Oh, he's.
噢，他确实是。

357
00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:38.820
That deer in headlights is real.
那种目瞪口呆的样子是真实的。

358
00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.640
I was like, oh, my God.
我当时心想，天哪。

359
00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:41.560
Okay.
好吧。

360
00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:41.940
Yeah.
是啊。

361
00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:42.240
Right.
没错。

362
00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:42.660
Of course.
当然。

363
00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:44.040
Oh, now I get the scene.
噢，我现在明白那场戏了。

364
00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:49.700
But that was really, that was so sweet and powerful.
但那真的很棒，既温馨又感人。

365
00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:50.720
Yeah.
是啊。

366
00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:52.100
And we were all crying.
我们当时都哭了。

367
00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:53.920
We were all looking at you.
我们都在看着你。

368
00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:54.160
Yeah.
是啊。

369
00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:56.240
Because you were standing in the front of the room with Steve.
因为你当时和史蒂夫一起站在房间前面。

370
00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:57.660
And we were all looking at you crying.
我们都在看着你哭。

371
00:12:57.780 --> 00:12:57.980
Yeah.
是啊。

372
00:12:57.980 --> 00:12:59.620
I am just now in this moment.
我此刻正沉浸在那种情绪里。

373
00:12:59.760 --> 00:12:59.920
Yeah.
是啊。

374
00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:04.820
Like putting myself in your shoes and imagining what it must have been like for you to stand
就像设身处地地想象一下，当时站在那里，

375
00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:06.880
there and Steve is crying next to you.
史蒂夫在你身边哭泣，那对你来说会是什么样的感受。

376
00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:07.880
We're all crying.
我们都在哭。

377
00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:09.260
And you're just like, hey.
而你却表现得像，嘿。

378
00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:16.300
And then as D'Angelo Vickers, who has no emotional attachment, then the more takes we did, then
然后作为迪安杰洛·维克斯，他本没有情感寄托，但随着我们拍摄的次数增多，

379
00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:19.240
I started, it started getting to me too.
我也开始，我也开始被感染了。

380
00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:19.580
Right.
没错。

381
00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:21.680
And you're like, D'Angelo can't cry here.
你当时心想，迪安杰洛不能在这里哭。

382
00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:22.920
D'Angelo can't cry here.
迪安杰洛不能在这里哭。

383
00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:25.200
He doesn't, he doesn't have anything invested.
他没有，他没有投入任何感情。

384
00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:27.660
Here's another fan question.
这是另一个粉丝提问。

385
00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:27.920
Okay.
好的。

386
00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.340
This is from Shell F.
来自Shell F。

387
00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:32.060
Had you watched the show before you came on?
你在加入剧组之前看过这部剧吗？

388
00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:33.000
Yes.
看过。

389
00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:42.180
I had watched the show many a time and yeah, I was a fan like everyone else and just loved,
我看过很多次，是的，我和其他人一样是粉丝，非常喜欢，

390
00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:47.620
you know, all, all the stuff everyone was doing and all the, the writing and the caSt.
你知道，大家所做的一切，所有的剧本和演员阵容。

391
00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:52.360
And just, as you guys know, kind of a perfect storm of all those things put together, which
正如你们所知，这简直是所有这些因素完美结合的产物，

392
00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:57.840
is why the combination of that and knowing Steve, but all of those things were the reason
所以这就是为什么，再加上认识史蒂夫，所有这些原因，

393
00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:58.840
why I called up.
让我打了那个电话。

394
00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.920
I was like, gosh, would they, would they fit me in?
我当时心想，天哪，他们会，他们会让我加入吗？

395
00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.280
And you guys did.
而你们确实让我加入了。

396
00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:05.860
And you got to go play with one of your best friends.
而且你还能和最好的朋友之一一起演戏。

397
00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:06.580
Yeah, exactly.
是的，没错。

398
00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:07.120
Yeah.
是啊。

399
00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:07.680
Exactly.
没错。

400
00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:12.760
And that was so fun to revisiting the episodes.
重温这些剧集真是太有趣了。

401
00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.860
I had totally forgotten that firSt.
我完全忘了那第一次了。

402
00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:20.380
The first meeting between Michael and D'Angelo.
迈克尔和安杰洛的第一次见面。

403
00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:23.940
Where we're at the bar and calling each other and we don't realize it.
我们在酒吧里互相打电话，却没意识到对方就在那儿。

404
00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:26.900
And it was like, I was watching them all for the first time.
当时就像是在第一次看他们演戏一样。

405
00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:29.640
It was just so fun to see how well constructed that was.
看到那段戏的结构如此精巧，真的太有意思了。

406
00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.640
And just, yeah, so stupid.
而且，就是，没错，太蠢了。

407
00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:33.260
Right?
对吧？

408
00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:33.840
Yeah.
是啊。

409
00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:34.420
Yeah.
没错。

410
00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:35.040
Okay.
好吧。

411
00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:37.300
This is actually a great time for me to share this with you.
现在正好是个好时机，可以跟你们分享一下。

412
00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:41.660
I saw online a list of fan favorite quotes from D'Angelo.
我在网上看到了一份粉丝最喜欢的安杰洛语录列表。

413
00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.560
Here are some really good ones.
这里有一些真的很棒的。

414
00:14:44.140 --> 00:14:45.100
Top of the liSt.
榜首。

415
00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:47.080
Colorado, the sunshine state.
科罗拉多，阳光之州。

416
00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:47.460
Yes.
没错。

417
00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:51.200
That baby could be the star of a show called Babies I Don't Care About.
那婴儿完全可以去演一部叫《我不在乎的婴儿》的剧。

418
00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:55.160
Everyone I know who skis is dead.
我认识的滑雪的人都死了。

419
00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:58.340
I never touch another juggler's instruments.
我从不碰其他杂耍艺人的道具。

420
00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:01.220
And then, is there an animal shelter on the way?
还有，路上有动物收容所吗？

421
00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:02.220
Annie Annie Shelto.
安妮·安妮·谢尔托。

422
00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:10.220
You know what's really fun about having done those four shows is the gift that keeps on giving,
你知道拍那四集节目最有趣的地方在于，它是一份持续不断的礼物，

423
00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:20.600
which is the, you know, Greg and Paul obviously thought of that bit of the juggling without my juggling apparatus.
那就是，格雷格和保罗显然想出了那个没有杂耍道具的杂耍桥段。

424
00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.880
We got more mail about that scene.
我们收到了很多关于那场戏的邮件。

425
00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:23.640
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

426
00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:27.060
People want to hear everything you have to say about the juggling.
大家想听听你对那段杂耍的所有想法。

427
00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:32.100
But I remember thinking, how and why did you guys think of it this way?
但我记得当时在想，你们是怎么想到这种方式的，为什么要这么做？

428
00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:40.340
I forget what their reason was, but that was just such a genius weirdo thing that he still wants to show off his juggling.
我忘了他们的理由是什么了，但这真是个天才般的怪点子，他居然还想炫耀他的杂耍技术。

429
00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:41.440
Yes.
没错。

430
00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:41.920
Yeah.
是啊。

431
00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:42.880
He had his book box.
他带着他的书箱。

432
00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:43.540
Without any juggling.
里面什么杂耍道具都没有。

433
00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:44.080
Yes.
对。

434
00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:51.440
And I have now done that bit on stage no less than 20 times.
我现在已经在舞台上表演过不下20次那个桥段了。

435
00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:51.960
Really?
真的吗？

436
00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:54.320
Because it's like a go-to.
因为这就像是我的拿手好戏。

437
00:15:56.500 --> 00:16:04.560
Because, you know, people will have like a little charity show or this and that where it's like, would you come do a five-minute thing or whatever you want to do?
因为，你知道，人们会办些小型慈善演出之类的，问我能不能去表演个五分钟，或者随便演点什么？

438
00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:06.860
It's like ready-made.
这就像是现成的节目。

439
00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:07.480
Yeah.
没错。

440
00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:07.840
It's perfect.
太完美了。

441
00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:17.980
So I'll come out and I'll say, just introduce me as so-and-so and that I'm a juggler who's worked for 20 years down at Fisherman's Worth in San Francisco or something.
所以我上台后会说，就介绍我是某某某，说我是在旧金山渔人码头表演了20年的杂耍艺人，之类的。

442
00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:19.440
So I come out.
然后我上台。

443
00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:21.660
I do the whole thing of like, I'm so sorry.
我演整套戏，比如，我太抱歉了。

444
00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:22.640
I left.
我把东西落下了。

445
00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:24.360
I have a little case.
我有个小箱子。

446
00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.000
I'll open up and there'll be nothing in there.
我会打开它，里面什么都没有。

447
00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:26.700
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

448
00:16:26.780 --> 00:16:27.540
What's happened to them?
它们去哪儿了？

449
00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.200
I'm so embarrassed.
我太尴尬了。

450
00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:31.340
All my juggling balls, I left them in my other case.
我所有的杂耍球，都落在另一个箱子里了。

451
00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:32.560
I don't know what to do.
我不知道该怎么办。

452
00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:34.780
And then coax the audience.
然后去哄观众。

453
00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:37.620
I'm like, unless I could just do my act without them and then everyone applauds.
我就想，除非我能撇开他们直接表演，然后大家都会鼓掌。

454
00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:38.220
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

455
00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:39.320
And I do the whole thing.
然后我把整套动作做完。

456
00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.600
Do you do the balls invisibly on someone's head?
你是要在别人的头上变隐形球吗？

457
00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:42.880
Yes.
是的。

458
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:43.460
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

459
00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:44.380
I'll pull someone out of the audience.
我会从观众席里拉一个人上来。

460
00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:45.200
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

461
00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:46.840
And then I'll do that.
然后我就做那个动作。

462
00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:50.380
I believe that defies like physics and gravity.
我觉得那违背了物理学和重力定律。

463
00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:51.940
It's not a possible move.
那是不可能完成的动作。

464
00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:54.600
And I whisper to them like, stay as still as you can.
我会悄悄对他们说，尽量保持不动。

465
00:16:56.420 --> 00:16:58.460
And people will take it really seriously.
人们会非常认真地对待。

466
00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:00.560
And they'll sit in the chair and they won't blink.
他们会坐在椅子上，连眼睛都不眨一下。

467
00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:02.980
And I'll just throw the balls off the head.
然后我就把球从他们头上扔出去。

468
00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:08.200
And I play the same Evanescence song.
我还放着同一首伊凡塞斯乐队的歌。

469
00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:09.100
I do the whole thing.
我把整套做完。

470
00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:09.400
Anyway.
总之。

471
00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:10.360
That is amazing.
那太棒了。

472
00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.680
It's the gift that keeps on giving.
这真是个源源不断的惊喜。

473
00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:12.920
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

474
00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:16.840
My favorite part of it is at the end when it lands on the back of your head.
我最喜欢的部分是最后球落在你后脑勺上的时候。

475
00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:17.240
Yes.
是的。

476
00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:17.740
Yes.
是的。

477
00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:18.800
You're going to catch it there.
你会在那里接住它。

478
00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:22.020
And Kevin's like, didn't drop a single ball.
凯文就会说，一个球都没掉。

479
00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:23.220
Right.
没错。

480
00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:28.240
So that was a highlight for sure.
那绝对是个高光时刻。

481
00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:29.060
Yeah.
是啊。

482
00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:29.320
For me.
对我来说。

483
00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:35.380
But also to just have to force you guys to watch it all for how many takes that I don't know.
但还得强迫你们看那么多次拍摄，我也不知道拍了多少遍。

484
00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:38.920
I saw myself breaking in so many takes with you.
我看到自己在和你搭档时笑场了好多次。

485
00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:39.300
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

486
00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:39.660
So many.
太多次了。

487
00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:40.160
I would see.
我看得出来。

488
00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:42.480
And also, not just me, but you would see shoulders.
而且不只是我，你也能看到肩膀。

489
00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:44.140
Like, shoulders are the dead giveaway.
肩膀的抖动最容易露馅。

490
00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:46.540
And we were cracking up.
我们当时都笑疯了。

491
00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:50.900
And then I just wanted to know, and we had people write in, have you ever juggled?
然后我就是想知道，我们收到了观众来信，问你有没有玩过杂耍？

492
00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:52.460
Do you know anything about juggling?
你对杂耍有什么了解吗？

493
00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:52.620
No.
没有。

494
00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:54.460
And I still can't juggle to this day.
直到今天我也不会玩杂耍。

495
00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:55.080
You can't.
你不会。

496
00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:56.840
You're such a good fake juggler.
你真是个优秀的杂耍骗子。

497
00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:56.960
Yeah.
是啊。

498
00:17:57.120 --> 00:18:02.620
It didn't give me, well, it didn't like spur me on to like, maybe I should really try juggling.
这并没有让我，嗯，并没有激励我产生“也许我真的该试试杂耍”的想法。

499
00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:03.960
Like, and just pretend.
就像，只是假装一下。

500
00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:05.340
Like, I'm faking it pretty well.
你看，我装得还挺像的。

501
00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:06.840
I still can't do it.
我还是做不到。

502
00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:08.180
I still haven't tried.
我还没试过呢。

503
00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:09.080
I still can't do it.
我还是做不到。

504
00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:10.220
Oh, you know what?
噢，你知道吗？

505
00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:11.720
We have talked about this.
我们讨论过这个。

506
00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:17.580
Your character has such a great way that he introduces himself to everyone in the bullpen.
你的角色向办公室里的每个人自我介绍的方式真是太棒了。

507
00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:19.640
And we really wanted you to hear it.
我们真的很想让你听听。

508
00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:24.600
And then Jenna's going to share with you a second part that didn't make it in that we found in the shooting draft.
然后珍娜会和你分享第二部分，那是我们在拍摄剧本里发现的，但没用上。

509
00:18:24.760 --> 00:18:24.980
Okay.
好的。

510
00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:29.280
Presenting D'Angelo Vickers.
隆重介绍迪安杰洛·维克斯。

511
00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:32.040
Hi.
嗨。

512
00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:33.300
Hello.
你好。

513
00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:40.890
How are you, sir?
你好吗，先生？

514
00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:41.530
I'm well, sir.
我很好，先生。

515
00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:42.010
How are you?
你呢？

516
00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:45.730
Can I just say I am so excited to be working here.
我能说我非常高兴能在这里工作吗。

517
00:18:46.010 --> 00:18:47.010
A little bit about myself.
简单介绍一下我自己。

518
00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:50.190
I love the American Southwest, for starters.
首先，我热爱美国西南部。

519
00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:53.650
You may call them Arizona, New Mexico, Nevada, Utah.
你们可能称之为亚利桑那州、新墨西哥州、内华达州、犹他州。

520
00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:55.250
I call them heaven.
我称之为天堂。

521
00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:56.530
I have a peanut allergy.
我对花生过敏。

522
00:18:56.890 --> 00:18:58.010
It's something I live with.
这是我生活的一部分。

523
00:18:58.250 --> 00:18:59.090
It's a part of me.
这是我的一部分。

524
00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:00.410
I've learned to cope with it.
我已经学会了如何应对它。

525
00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:00.950
