00:48:04.340 --> 00:48:04.920
Stop it.
别说了。

1400
00:48:05.320 --> 00:48:06.420
I have a good ending.
我有个好的结尾。

1401
00:48:06.460 --> 00:48:08.280
I sure, there's going to be, you're going to get so many letters.
我敢肯定，会有很多人写信给你的。

1402
00:48:08.640 --> 00:48:08.840
No, no.
不，不。

1403
00:48:09.040 --> 00:48:09.560
Dud City.
烂透了。

1404
00:48:09.900 --> 00:48:10.680
By the way, Steve said.
顺便说一下，史蒂夫说了。

1405
00:48:10.680 --> 00:48:11.900
By the way, Farrell, Dud City.
顺便说一下，法瑞尔，烂透了。

1406
00:48:12.100 --> 00:48:13.080
Steve was like.
史蒂夫当时说。

1407
00:48:13.080 --> 00:48:14.640
Dud City, hashtag Dud City USA.
烂透了，标签：美国烂透了。

1408
00:48:14.940 --> 00:48:19.060
When we did Steve's regular guy questions, all we did was make Steve feel like he was the
当我们做史蒂夫的“普通人问答”时，我们只是让史蒂夫觉得他是

1409
00:48:19.060 --> 00:48:20.200
most boring person on earth.
地球上最无聊的人。

1410
00:48:20.220 --> 00:48:20.720
He was like, oh my God.
他当时说，哦，天哪。

1411
00:48:20.720 --> 00:48:22.980
He was like, I am, why did Nancy marry me?
他当时说，我是，南希为什么要嫁给我？

1412
00:48:24.960 --> 00:48:29.580
Like, I'm hearing myself back and I've never felt worse about myself.
就像是，我听着自己的回放，从来没觉得这么糟糕过。

1413
00:48:29.940 --> 00:48:32.360
This is why we asked to take the picture at the top.
这就是为什么我们要求在开头拍那张照片。

1414
00:48:32.480 --> 00:48:36.120
Maybe we should leave people in like a shame spiral.
也许我们应该让人们陷入羞愧的漩涡中。

1415
00:48:36.560 --> 00:48:37.140
You knew it was prophetic.
你当时就知道这很有预见性。

1416
00:48:37.140 --> 00:48:41.820
We might need to change the name from regular guy quiz to just like, want to feel shitty?
我们可能需要把“普通人问答”改名叫“想感觉糟糕吗？”

1417
00:48:44.480 --> 00:48:46.460
Want to really feel.
想真的感觉一下吗。

1418
00:48:48.340 --> 00:48:53.500
Now I got to get a hobby so I can literally answer this question.
现在我得找个爱好，这样我才能真正回答这个问题。

1419
00:48:54.160 --> 00:48:56.680
We want to thank you so much for coming today, Will.
威尔，非常感谢你今天能来。

1420
00:48:56.820 --> 00:49:01.260
And I wanted to end with this, such this sweet note from a fan, from Maxie B.
我想以这个结尾，来自粉丝Maxie B.的一封非常贴心的信。

1421
00:49:02.360 --> 00:49:07.660
Maxie said this, my mom and I adore watching Will Ferrell movies together and cracking up.
Maxie是这么说的：我和我妈妈非常喜欢一起看威尔·法瑞尔的电影，总是笑得前仰后合。

1422
00:49:07.780 --> 00:49:12.640
My mom just turned 70 in January and we began talking about the thing that all kids dread
我妈妈一月份刚满70岁，我们开始谈论所有孩子都害怕

1423
00:49:12.640 --> 00:49:15.460
talking about with their parents, the funeral arrangements.
与父母谈论的事情，葬礼安排。

1424
00:49:16.060 --> 00:49:21.380
She wants cremation and a big party to celebrate her life, which I love, but she had the cutest
她想要火葬，并举办一场盛大的派对来庆祝她的一生，我很喜欢这个想法，但她有一个最可爱的

1425
00:49:21.380 --> 00:49:23.720
request that she knows won't be able to happen.
请求，她知道这不可能实现。

1426
00:49:24.440 --> 00:49:29.620
She asked me to please hire Will Ferrell to sing her favorite song, Dust in the Wind, at
她让我一定要请威尔·法瑞尔在她的派对上唱她最喜欢的歌《尘归尘》（Dust in the Wind）。

1427
00:49:29.620 --> 00:49:30.380
her party.
她的派对上。

1428
00:49:30.760 --> 00:49:32.880
I just think that is the sweetest thing.
我觉得这真是太贴心了。

1429
00:49:33.000 --> 00:49:36.080
And I would love for Will to know how much he means to us and our family.
我非常希望威尔能知道他对我们和我们的家庭有多重要。

1430
00:49:36.280 --> 00:49:38.300
He has kept us going through hard times.
他在我们度过困难时期时一直支撑着我们。

1431
00:49:38.440 --> 00:49:40.640
All my love, Maxie B.
爱你的，Maxie B.

1432
00:49:40.900 --> 00:49:41.280
Wow.
哇。

1433
00:49:41.860 --> 00:49:43.120
Isn't that so sweet?
这不是很贴心吗？

1434
00:49:43.400 --> 00:49:43.450
That's so great.
太棒了。

1435
00:49:45.460 --> 00:49:52.040
You bring so much comfort to people with what you do, with your comedy, and just with who
你所做的一切，你的喜剧，以及你这个人本身，给人们带来了极大的慰藉。

1436
00:49:52.040 --> 00:49:52.600
you are.
你本身。

1437
00:49:52.820 --> 00:49:57.120
You brought so much comfort to us on The Office when you came in during that transition time.
你在《办公室》过渡时期加入时，也给我们带来了极大的慰藉。

1438
00:49:57.680 --> 00:49:59.220
So, I mean, that's why we do it.
所以，我的意思是，这就是我们做这件事的原因。

1439
00:49:59.300 --> 00:50:01.760
That's why, I mean, that's what being an artist is.
这就是，我的意思是，这就是身为艺术家的意义所在。

1440
00:50:01.980 --> 00:50:03.660
That couldn't be nicer.
这真是再好不过了。

1441
00:50:04.080 --> 00:50:04.520
Nicer.
更好。

1442
00:50:04.580 --> 00:50:06.560
And what a fun sense of humor her mom has.
而且她妈妈的幽默感真有趣。

1443
00:50:06.560 --> 00:50:06.800
Yeah.
是啊。

1444
00:50:06.800 --> 00:50:09.480
She wants to be cremated and wants you to sing Dust in the Wind.
她想火葬，还想让你唱《尘归尘》。

1445
00:50:09.740 --> 00:50:11.200
I love this woman.
我爱这位女士。

1446
00:50:11.540 --> 00:50:11.980
Right?
对吧？

1447
00:50:12.280 --> 00:50:12.800
I know.
我知道。

1448
00:50:13.040 --> 00:50:13.420
I know.
我知道。

1449
00:50:13.820 --> 00:50:14.560
I'm speechless.
我无言以对。

1450
00:50:14.760 --> 00:50:15.680
We adore you.
我们崇拜你。

1451
00:50:15.860 --> 00:50:16.440
We really do.
我们确实是这么想的。

1452
00:50:16.620 --> 00:50:20.800
I'm just always so happy when I see you and when we run into you, you're just one of the
每次见到你，或者偶然遇见你，我总是特别开心，你真的是那种

1453
00:50:20.800 --> 00:50:21.220
good guys.
好人。

1454
00:50:21.480 --> 00:50:21.660
Oh, thanks.
噢，谢谢。

1455
00:50:21.660 --> 00:50:22.240
You're one of the good ones.
你是个好人。

1456
00:50:23.060 --> 00:50:23.960
Thanks, you guys.
谢谢你们。

1457
00:50:24.220 --> 00:50:24.820
Thank you.
谢谢。

1458
00:50:24.820 --> 00:50:24.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

1459
00:50:24.960 --> 00:50:25.340
Thank you.
谢谢。

1460
00:50:25.340 --> 00:50:28.680
I'm just going to drive in my car now.
我现在只想开车兜兜风。

1461
00:50:31.600 --> 00:50:32.080
Yeah.
是啊。

1462
00:50:32.080 --> 00:50:32.780
You know what?
你知道吗？

1463
00:50:32.880 --> 00:50:35.520
And just let all of this praise wash over me.
让这些赞美之词洗礼我吧。

1464
00:50:36.080 --> 00:50:36.540
Own it.
尽情享受吧。

1465
00:50:36.760 --> 00:50:36.980
Okay.
好的。

1466
00:50:37.240 --> 00:50:40.480
That was so much fun.
真是太有趣了。

1467
00:50:40.620 --> 00:50:41.540
So fun.
太好玩了。

1468
00:50:41.880 --> 00:50:42.300
Okay.
好的。

1469
00:50:42.460 --> 00:50:46.900
Before we leave for our two-week break, you guys, you know how much I love birthdays.
在我们开始两周假期之前，伙计们，你们知道我有多爱过生日。

1470
00:50:47.120 --> 00:50:48.920
You know how much I love celebrating them.
你们知道我有多喜欢庆祝生日。

1471
00:50:49.100 --> 00:50:51.980
Well, we have had a wonky few weeks with scheduling.
好吧，这几周我们的日程安排有点乱。

1472
00:50:51.980 --> 00:50:56.340
We've had a lot going on, and we were not able to celebrate Jenna's birthday.
我们事情太多了，没能给珍娜庆祝生日。

1473
00:50:56.340 --> 00:50:59.300
Wednesday, when it was her birthday week, but you know what?
周三本来是她的生日周，但你知道吗？

1474
00:50:59.620 --> 00:51:02.140
It is never too late for birthday week.
生日周永远不会太迟。

1475
00:51:02.300 --> 00:51:04.820
I am honestly, I am surprised.
说实话，我很惊讶。

1476
00:51:05.240 --> 00:51:06.060
This is so nice.
这太好了。

1477
00:51:06.820 --> 00:51:11.580
Angela, you know, I spent my birthday by myself in New York City because I was shooting
安吉拉，你知道，我生日那天是一个人在纽约市过的，因为我在拍

1478
00:51:11.580 --> 00:51:12.120
Mean Girls.
《贱女孩》。

1479
00:51:12.120 --> 00:51:12.760
I know.
我知道。

1480
00:51:13.100 --> 00:51:15.080
And it was a little tough.
那确实有点难熬。

1481
00:51:15.080 --> 00:51:16.840
I'll say my family was wonderful.
我得说我的家人真的很棒。

1482
00:51:17.100 --> 00:51:22.420
Lee hid birthday presents in my suitcase for me to open, and we celebrated a little before
李把生日礼物藏在我的行李箱里让我打开，我在离开前庆祝了一下，

1483
00:51:22.420 --> 00:51:24.600
I left, a little bit after I got home.
回家后又庆祝了一点。

1484
00:51:24.600 --> 00:51:28.180
But we have not been able to celebrate here on the pod.
但我们还没能在播客里庆祝过。

1485
00:51:28.780 --> 00:51:30.260
So ladies, sit back.
所以女士们，坐好。

1486
00:51:30.480 --> 00:51:32.160
I got some stuff coming your way.
我有东西要给你们。

1487
00:51:32.300 --> 00:51:32.920
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1488
00:51:33.040 --> 00:51:36.320
Cody and Sam, I'm opening up the shower screen door thing.
科迪和萨姆，我要打开淋浴屏风门了。

1489
00:51:36.920 --> 00:51:39.780
Cassie, I'm sad you're not here today, but we'll save some for you.
凯西，我很遗憾你今天不在，但我们会给你留一些的。

1490
00:51:41.500 --> 00:51:41.940
Okay.
好的。

1491
00:51:42.120 --> 00:51:45.480
I had this all hidden in the corner of the room.
我把这些都藏在房间角落里了。

1492
00:51:45.560 --> 00:51:46.840
I had no idea this was here.
我完全不知道这里有东西。

1493
00:51:46.840 --> 00:51:47.220
Okay.
好的。

1494
00:51:47.460 --> 00:51:51.940
So first of all, this is a gift that the minute you open it, it's something you said
首先，这是一份礼物，你打开它的那一刻，就会发现它是你

1495
00:51:51.940 --> 00:51:52.420
you wanted.
说想要的东西。

1496
00:51:52.420 --> 00:51:52.900
Okay.
好的。

1497
00:51:53.160 --> 00:51:53.580
Okay.
好的。

1498
00:51:54.140 --> 00:51:55.600
Something I said I wanted.
我曾说我想要的东西。

1499
00:51:56.020 --> 00:52:02.400
I want this.
我想要这个。

1500
00:52:02.700 --> 00:52:09.360
This is the lighted magnification mirror so I can tweeze my eyebrows.
这是带灯的放大镜，这样我就能修眉毛了。

1501
00:52:09.520 --> 00:52:13.840
And it magnifies three times the magnitude of whatever.
它能把任何东西放大三倍。

1502
00:52:14.120 --> 00:52:16.100
My 49 year old eyes.
我这49岁的眼睛。

1503
00:52:16.300 --> 00:52:17.400
Thank you so much.
太感谢你了。

1504
00:52:17.440 --> 00:52:19.060
Wait, I have to take your picture with it.
等等，我得用它给你拍张照。

1505
00:52:20.140 --> 00:52:20.700
Okay.
好的。

1506
00:52:21.080 --> 00:52:25.260
And next lady, I went to one of my favorite bakeries and I got you gluten-free brownies
接下来这位女士，我去了我最喜欢的一家烘焙店，给你买了无麸质布朗尼

1507
00:52:25.260 --> 00:52:26.160
with sprinkles.
上面还有糖针。

1508
00:52:26.480 --> 00:52:28.700
Ooh, gluten-free dessert.
噢，无麸质甜点。

1509
00:52:29.740 --> 00:52:31.440
Oh, I love it.
噢，我太喜欢了。

1510
00:52:31.780 --> 00:52:32.140
Okay.
好的。

1511
00:52:32.340 --> 00:52:34.280
I hope they didn't get tossed around in the car.
希望它们在车里没被颠坏。

1512
00:52:35.340 --> 00:52:36.620
Oh, they're perfect.
噢，它们完好无损。

1513
00:52:37.160 --> 00:52:38.560
Thank you, lady.
谢谢你，女士。

1514
00:52:39.000 --> 00:52:39.260
Happy birthday.
生日快乐。

1515
00:52:42.130 --> 00:52:43.250
Bye, you guys.
再见，伙计们。

1516
00:52:43.250 --> 00:52:43.690
Bye.
再见。

1517
00:52:43.970 --> 00:52:44.890
See you in two weeks.
两周后再见。

